  "obligation": "Execute unshared struct.get, struct.get_s, struct.get_u and struct.set through the single VM, preserving packed storage, field identity, mutability and null traps.",
  "representation": "The validator resolves static source types and subtype prefixes preserve packed storage/mutable-field invariance. Residual instructions retain only the field index; the original live object declaration owns layout. One StructFieldAccess domain maps access to opcodes and checks admissible storage/mutability. Construction and mutation share wasm_storage_value for packed truncation and typed reference/scalar validation. Reads preserve Values or sign-extend packed integers. Four appended opcodes use existing registers and heap; no extra cells, side maps or copied layouts.",
  "scope": "230 matching affected pinned files and45 focused files. New15-directive controls cover signed/unsigned i8/i16 values and truncation, immutable f32 negative zero, i64 minimum, reference identity and retention across50000 allocations, field index300, shifted equivalent foreign declarations, null traps and operand side effects before a null setter trap. No full suite.",
